# Phase 5 L-U2: a stop after a finished turn clears the record, and the
# resume reports again -- idle, because the result was already reported.
# Under `jobctl`, so a stop really stops. fx stops on a typed Ctrl-Z
# (`app_input_runtime.zig:862-866`); a typed Ctrl-Z binds nothing in xfx
# (docs/parity.md, the full-screen TUI row), whose stop is a SIGTSTP, so each
# product is stopped its own way and both are continued with SIGCONT.
gateway p5-lifecycle-one-turn.json
jobctl
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 4
type first question
key Enter
wait 3
wire s00-done
fx: key C-z
xfx: signal TSTP
wait 1
wire s01-stopped
signal CONT
wait 2
wire s02-resumed
type second question
key Enter
wait 3
wire s03-next-turn
